Authoritative benchmark
-----------------------
The chronologically first complete locked final-source run is authoritative.
Builds finished by 2026-07-20T07:24:25Z.  Lock acquisition was 07:24:35Z,
before the pre-run endpoint audit; release was 07:26:26Z after the post-run
endpoint audit.  Both endpoint snapshots found no m2clasetforce process.
The lock excludes overlapping cooperating driver invocations only; endpoint
snapshots do not establish absence of unrelated/manual processes throughout.
Every row had status 0 and reconstruction_interrupted under the unchanged
30-second shared cooperative deadline and 60-second watchdog.

The original completion-only validator rejected this same authoritative raw
capture because valid cutoff prefixes need not have equal adjacent phase
entry counts.  The identical rejected raw/audit are retained as diagnostics.
A later complete locked replication audit and extracted stdout/status ledger
are retained and explicitly non-authoritative.  Its full marker raw was
overwritten before the stop-selection-bias direction arrived and is not
claimed retained.  No authoritative run was selected for a convenient cutoff.

The authoritative `process-audit.txt` is restored byte-for-byte from the
22-line `rejected-schema-process-audit.txt`; `cmp` exits 0.  The previously
current 29-line ledger is preserved without alteration as
`contaminated-appended-process-audit.txt`.  It consists of the authoritative
22 lines followed by a 07:32:07 post-run endpoint/release block.  The retained
evidence does not identify the process or mechanism that appended that block,
so the contamination cause is unknown.  The manifest labels and hashes the
authoritative, contaminated, rejected-schema and later-replication artifacts.

Mechanical validation
---------------------
verify-claset-force.awk checks exact schema/order/status/observer identities,
exact phase/kind subtotals, entry/exit and non-nested forcing-prefix relations,
coherent absent/concrete stored context, major-at-most-minor, SafeRule
non-duplication, and positive current outer/stored boundary counts.  It does
not require completion equalities and does not purport to reject every
semantically impossible state.  Each fixed-order problem block requires its
exact one/three/one attempt-enter/result pairs before its sole stdout; no
active/missing attempt or later marker is allowed.  The one status row follows
stdout and terminates the block.  Fixed positive schedule/control numerals are
canonical `[1-9][0-9]*` lexemes equal to their scheduled literals, and status
is exactly `0`.  Elapsed seconds accept `[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?` in `[30,60)`;
arbitrary natural counters remain `[0-9]+`, including leading zeroes.  It also
checks:
  stop_polls = search cooperative checkpoints +
               sum(reconstruction cooperative checkpoints).
test-validator.sh: exit 0; attempts.tsv reproduced exactly.  The synthetic
pre-stored interruption and all eleven classical phases at Enter and Exit
(23 positive cases total) were accepted.  bad-header, unknown-phase,
reordered-record, bad-stdout, bad-status, bad-counter, bad-global-poll,
bad-prefix and bad-entry-balance were retained and rejected with diagnostics.
Six generated-and-retained negatives for major-over-minor, SafeRule
duplication, partial and absent-but-counted stored context, and bad
outer/stored current counts reproduced byte-for-byte and rejected with
diagnostics (15 prior negative cases total).  Six new generated-and-retained
fixtures for stdout before any attempt/result completion, marker after stdout,
and noncanonical run/attempt/status numerals also reproduced byte-for-byte and
rejected with diagnostics (21 negative cases total).

